# Placeholder for SSL certificates
# 
# For production deployment:
# 1. Obtain SSL certificate (Let's Encrypt, AWS Certificate Manager, etc.)
# 2. Place certificate files here:
#    - cert.pem (full chain certificate)
#    - key.pem (private key)
# 3. Update nginx/conf.d/default.conf to enable HTTPS server block
#
# For Let's Encrypt with certbot:
# certbot certonly --standalone -d your-domain.com -d www.your-domain.com
# Then copy files from /etc/letsencrypt/live/your-domain.com/ to this directory
